  "stem": "The function \\(f\\) is defined by \\(f(x) = 10x - 1\\). What is the value of \\(f\\left(\\frac{1}{2}\\right)\\)?",
  "figure": null,
  "answer_type": "mcq",
  "choices": {
    "A": "\\(4\\)",
    "B": "\\(5\\)",
    "C": "\\(19\\)",
    "D": "\\(\\frac{9}{2}\\)"
  },
  "answer": "A",
  "spr_answers": null,
  "solution": [
    "Substitute \\(x = \\frac{1}{2}\\): \\(f\\left(\\frac{1}{2}\\right) = 10 \\cdot \\frac{1}{2} - 1\\).",
    "\\(10 \\cdot \\frac{1}{2} = 5\\), so the value is \\(5 - 1 = 4\\)."
  ],
  "explanation": {
    "A": "Correct. \\(10 \\cdot \\frac{1}{2} = 5\\), and \\(5 - 1 = 4\\).",
    "B": "Incorrect. This is \\(10 \\cdot \\frac{1}{2}\\) without subtracting 1.",
    "C": "Incorrect. This is \\(f(2) = 10(2) - 1\\); the input is \\(\\frac{1}{2}\\), not 2.",
    "D": "Incorrect. This computes \\((10 - 1) \\cdot \\frac{1}{2}\\); only \\(10\\) is multiplied by \\(\\frac{1}{2}\\)."
  },
